---
const buckets = [
  {
    name: 'Reachability',
    body:
      'ssh $DISCOBOX_ID works the moment you run discobox admin ssh-config --write. git, HTTP and ssh are proxied through the CLI, and HTTP services in the box are detected and forwarded to local ports.',
    line: '$ ssh purple-mongoose',
  },
  {
    name: 'Tool parity',
    body:
      'direnv is wired up, so nix, mise, or whatever your project already declares pulls your toolchain into the box on entry. Boxes launch in seconds with the agent ready to go.',
    line: 'direnv: loading .envrc · nix develop',
  },
  {
    name: 'Code flow',
    body:
      'Your source is cloned in. Commits come back out and are cherry-picked onto your working tree. Work leaves as commits, not as a diff you have to trust.',
    line: '$ discobox apply',
  },
  {
    name: 'Programmability',
    body:
      'A full OpenAPI surface and a scriptable CLI. Anything the TUI does, a shell script can do — including creating boxes, granting secrets, and collecting the results.',
    line: '$ discobox ls --output json',
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="using-it">
  <div class="page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Living with it</p>
    <p class="couplet__hook">The box is somewhere else. It should not feel like it.</p>
    <p class="couplet__turn">
      The reason you work on your laptop is that everything is already there. A remote
      machine gives that up. Most of Discobox is spent giving it back — and it is the
      same architecture doing it. Because every crossing goes through a channel
      Discobox controls, that channel can enforce policy on the way out and make the
      box feel local on the way in.
    </p>

    <div class="buckets">
      {
        buckets.map((bucket) => (
          <div class="card bucket">
            <h3 class="bucket__name">{bucket.name}</h3>
            <p class="bucket__body">{bucket.body}</p>
            <p class="bucket__line">{bucket.line}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .buckets {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .buckets {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  .bucket {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .bucket__name {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .bucket__body {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.96rem;
    flex: 1;
  }

  .bucket__line {
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
    padding-top: 0.9rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--magenta);
    overflow-x: auto;
    white-space: pre;
  }
</style>
